// wp_stream_threshold — the byte size at or below which a record is routed to
// the STRUCTURE stream; above it, to the PAYLOAD stream (S2).
//
// 32 bytes, chosen because the measured corpus is cleanly bimodal — structure
// records top out at 31 bytes and payload records start at 64 — so a size
// threshold and a type tag select exactly the same records. Routing on size
// keeps the write path free of any knowledge of what a record MEANS, which is
// the same reason it frames with a length prefix rather than a schema.
//
// This is a routing rule, not a format constant: a block written on either
// side decodes identically. Changing it changes which stream future records
// land in and nothing about the ones already durable.
fn wp_stream_threshold(_u: Unit) -> Int {
  Int(32)
}
